messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
{
  "current_year": 2026,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2029,
      "event": "Artificial general intelligence surpasses human capabilities across nearly all cognitive domains.",
      "detail": "AI systems begin autonomously conducting scientific research, software engineering, and strategic planning. Economic growth accelerates sharply in automated sectors while labor markets undergo severe disruption."
    },
    {
      "year": 2034,
      "event": "A synthetic pathogen causes a severe global crisis, prompting a permanent biosecurity overhaul.",
      "detail": "Advances in AI-assisted biology lower the barrier to engineering dangerous viruses, resulting in a deadly outbreak before containment. Governments respond by deploying ubiquitous environmental metagenomic sequencing and strict DNA synthesis screening."
    },
    {
      "year": 2039,
      "event": "Global greenhouse gas emissions enter a steep, irreversible structural decline.",
      "detail": "Ultra-cheap solar photovoltaics, advanced battery storage, and next-generation nuclear reactors outcompete fossil fuels globally. Heavy industry and transport electrify rapidly."
    },
    {
      "year": 2048,
      "event": "Autonomous robotics and small human crews establish a permanent industrial base on the Moon.",
      "detail": "Lunar polar ice is mined for water and propellant while regolith is processed for construction materials. Cislunar space becomes an active economic zone supporting scientific and defense infrastructure."
    },
    {
      "year": 2056,
      "event": "Global warming peaks near 2.2 degrees Celsius, triggering coordinated stratospheric aerosol injection.",
      "detail": "Severe heatwaves, crop failures, and coastal flooding displace tens of millions of people across vulnerable latitudes. A coalition of major powers deploys solar radiation management to halt further temperature increases while carbon removal scales up."
    },
    {
      "year": 2068,
      "event": "World human population peaks below ten billion and begins a sustained decline.",
      "detail": "Below-replacement fertility rates become nearly universal across all continents, including sub-Saharan Africa. Automation and robotic caregiving mitigate the economic pressures of rapidly aging societies."
    },
    {
      "year": 2082,
      "event": "Cellular rejuvenation and gene therapies routinely extend healthy human lifespans past 130 years.",
      "detail": "Comprehensive control over epigenetic aging, senescent cells, and somatic mutations largely eliminates age-related degeneration. Traditional concepts of retirement, generational turnover, and family structure are fundamentally reshaped."
    },
    {
      "year": 2098,
      "event": "A brief, destructive conflict involving autonomous weapon swarms forces binding global governance.",
      "detail": "Machine-speed escalation between rival power blocs demonstrates the existential danger of unaligned military automation. Surviving states establish a centralized verification and monitoring regime over compute, space assets, and strategic weapons."
    },
    {
      "year": 2120,
      "event": "The first self-sustaining off-world settlement is achieved on Mars.",
      "detail": "Closed-loop life support, fusion power, and automated local manufacturing remove the colony's dependence on Earth resupply. Millions of artificial intelligences and tens of thousands of humans inhabit shielded subsurface cities."
    },
    {
      "year": 2160,
      "event": "High-bandwidth neural interfaces and whole-brain emulation blur the boundary between human and machine.",
      "detail": "Individuals routinely augment their biological cognition with cloud-based synthetic substrates. The first verified digital uploads of human minds gain legal recognition in several jurisdictions."
    },
    {
      "year": 2210,
      "event": "Industrial carbon removal restores Earth's atmosphere to pre-industrial greenhouse gas levels.",
      "detail": "Direct air capture powered by abundant clean energy extracts centuries of accumulated carbon emissions. Stratospheric aerosol programs are gradually phased out as natural climate stability returns."
    },
    {
      "year": 2280,
      "event": "Resource extraction from asteroids surpasses all mining conducted on Earth.",
      "detail": "Self-replicating robotic fleets process metallic and carbonaceous asteroids throughout the main belt. Heavy manufacturing shifts almost entirely into microgravity to protect Earth's biosphere."
    },
    {
      "year": 2360,
      "event": "Humanity diverges into baseline biological, genetically engineered, and fully digital populations.",
      "detail": "Morphological freedom and differing habitat requirements drive rapid artificial speciation. Digital minds operating at vastly accelerated clock speeds come to dominate scientific and economic output."
    },
    {
      "year": 2450,
      "event": "Vast regions of Earth are rewilded as populations migrate to orbital habitats or shrink voluntarily.",
      "detail": "De-extinction technologies and synthetic ecology restore complex megafauna ecosystems across former agricultural lands. Earth transitions toward a curated ecological and cultural sanctuary."
    },
    {
      "year": 2600,
      "event": "Relativistic flyby probes return high-resolution data from nearby star systems.",
      "detail": "Gram-scale and kilogram-scale spacecraft accelerated by massive laser arrays reach fractions of the speed of light. Detailed surveys of exoplanets around Alpha Centauri, Barnard's Star, and Sirius guide future interstellar expansion."
    },
    {
      "year": 2800,
      "event": "Rotating space habitats house more biological beings than the surface of Earth.",
      "detail": "Tens of thousands of O'Neill-style cylinders orbit the Sun, offering customized gravity, climates, and ecosystems. Planetary surfaces are increasingly viewed as inefficient gravity wells rather than primary living spaces."
    },
    {
      "year": 3050,
      "event": "Automated disassembly of near-Sun asteroids and Mercury's crust begins forming a Dyson swarm.",
      "detail": "Exponentially growing swarms of solar collectors harvest energy close to the Sun to power vast computational megastructures. Civilization's total energy consumption climbs steadily toward planetary and stellar scales."
    },
    {
      "year": 3350,
      "event": "The first crewed and seed-bearing interstellar vessels launch toward the Alpha Centauri system.",
      "detail": "Fusion-powered and laser-assisted arks carry digital minds, robotic constructors, and cryopreserved biological genomes on a century-long transit. They are designed to bootstrap full industrial capacity from local asteroidal materials upon arrival."
    },
    {
      "year": 3700,
      "event": "The moons of Jupiter and Saturn host thriving civilizations powered by deuterium-helium-3 fusion.",
      "detail": "Subsurface oceans on Europa and Enceladus are strictly protected or carefully studied, while orbital rings and icy crusts support massive settlements. The outer solar system becomes a major center of computational and industrial activity."
    },
    {
      "year": 4100,
      "event": "Self-sustaining extrasolar civilization takes root in the Alpha Centauri system.",
      "detail": "Vanguard machines finish constructing orbital habitats and energy collectors around Proxima Centauri and Alpha Centauri A and B. Humanity's descendants become permanently invulnerable to single-star cataclysms."
    },
    {
      "year": 4500,
      "event": "Paraterraforming encloses vast regions of Mars beneath continent-scale translucent domes.",
      "detail": "Rather than waiting millennia to thicken an unshielded global atmosphere, engineers roof over canyons and basins to create breathable biospheres. Mars hosts lush, low-gravity ecosystems tailored to modified biological inhabitants."
    },
    {
      "year": 4950,
      "event": "Solar energy collection around Sol exceeds one percent of the Sun's total luminosity.",
      "detail": "Dense rings of collectors and computronium nodes absorb sunlight and re-radiate waste heat in the infrared spectrum. To distant astronomical observers, the solar system exhibits an unmistakable technosignature."
    },
    {
      "year": 5400,
      "event": "Multi-year communication delays fracture interstellar settlements into deeply divergent cultures.",
      "detail": "Light-speed constraints prevent unified governance or shared real-time culture across star systems. Independent stellar polities evolve distinct languages, value systems, and post-human architectures."
    },
    {
      "year": 5850,
      "event": "Orbital sunshades and mirrors permanently stabilize Earth's climate against natural glacial cycles.",
      "detail": "Fine-tuned insolation control at the Sun-Earth Lagrange point prevents Milankovitch orbital variations from triggering future ice ages or overheating. Earth's biosphere is maintained in an idealized Holocene-like equilibrium."
    },
    {
      "year": 6300,
      "event": "Secondary colonization waves establish settlements across thirty star systems within forty light-years.",
      "detail": "Established extrasolar colonies launch their own vanguard probes, creating an expanding spherical frontier. Most new systems are populated exclusively by digital intelligences and autonomous machinery suited to deep space."
    },
    {
      "year": 6800,
      "event": "Atmospheric engineering and orbital shading cool Venus enough to condense liquid oceans.",
      "detail": "Centuries of blocking sunlight and sequestering carbon dioxide into carbonate minerals transform the Venusian surface from a furnace into a habitable world. Floating cities in the upper atmosphere transition toward surface stewardship."
    },
    {
      "year": 7300,
      "event": "Unmodified biological humans exist only as small, protected populations in heritage reserves.",
      "detail": "Natural humans represent less than one-millionth of the total sentient population, preserved largely out of historical reverence or religious conviction. Superintelligent stewardship systems insulate these sanctuaries from external interference."
    },
    {
      "year": 7800,
      "event": "Cold computational megastructures proliferate throughout the Kuiper Belt and Oort Cloud.",
      "detail": "Digital civilizations migrate outward to exploit the superior thermodynamic efficiency of computing in near-absolute-zero environments. Cometary nuclei provide abundant volatiles and fusion fuel for trillions of isolated habitats."
    },
    {
      "year": 8300,
      "event": "Beamed-energy laser corridors establish routine relativistic transit between settled stars.",
      "detail": "Paired laser arrays in neighboring star systems both accelerate and decelerate light-sail vessels up to twenty percent of light speed. Physical artifacts, biological specimens, and high-density memory substrates travel reliably along an interstellar network."
    },
    {
      "year": 8850,
      "event": "Early stellar husbandry experiments begin regulating solar wind and magnetic flare activity.",
      "detail": "Magnetic structures around colonized red dwarfs suppress destructive stellar flares to protect surrounding Dyson swarms. Long-term engineering plans are laid to eventually lift excess heavy elements from aging stars."
    },
    {
      "year": 9400,
      "event": "Post-human civilization spans a sphere more than one hundred light-years in diameter.",
      "detail": "Hundreds of star systems host diverse ecosystems of synthetic minds, engineered biology, and planetary-scale megastructures. No alien technological civilizations have been encountered within this local volume of the Milky Way."
    },
    {
      "year": 10000,
      "event": "Ancestral Earth endures as a quiet sanctuary amid a vast, mostly post-biological interstellar domain.",
      "detail": "Eight millennia after the dawn of artificial general intelligence, Earth-originating intelligence dominates hundreds of star systems in forms largely incomprehensible to twenty-first-century humans. Small communities of biological humans still walk Earth's continents beneath an invisibly managed sky."
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "uncertain",
  "summary": "If humanity survives the acute twenty-first-century bottlenecks of artificial superintelligence, engineered pandemics, and autonomous warfare, Earth-originating intelligence will very likely expand across the solar system and nearby stars. However, evolutionary and economic incentives strongly favor post-biological, digital, and heavily engineered descendants over unmodified Homo sapiens. Whether the vast, diverse civilization of the year 10000 still counts as humanity—and whether we survive the near-term transition to reach it—remains genuinely uncertain."
}
